ential equation.\n\n$$\n2x{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+3y=0\n$$\n\nLet $y={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above.\nGiven that $\\lambda \\in (-2,-1),$ find the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,….$\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{″} & =2({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ 5{y}^{′} & =5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ 3y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{n(6n-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377419} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{n(n+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377420} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{n(6n+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377421} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{6n+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377422} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{n(6n+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{4{a}_{n-1}}{n(6n+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377423} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377418}] :question/math-academy-id "q-345165" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n6x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+4y=0\n$$\n\nLet $y={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above.\nGiven that $\\lambda \\in (\\frac{1}{2},1),$ find the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,….$\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x{y}^{″} & =6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ {y}^{′} & =\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ 4y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{n-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377426} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{n(n+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377427} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{n(n-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377428} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{(n-3)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377429} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{n(n-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n-1}}{n(n-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377428} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377425}] :question/math-academy-id "q-345166" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=0\n$$\n\nLet $y={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above.\nGiven that $\\lambda \\in (-4,-2),$ find the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,….$\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{″} & =({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ 4{y}^{′} & =4\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ 3y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Recurrence Formula for the Coefficients of a Frobenius Series Solution: Constant Coefficients of y and y'" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050111 :topic/math-academy-id 6727 :topic/title "Finding Recurrence Relations for the Coefficients of a Frobenius Solution"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231431 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231581 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n) = n(6n - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230353} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n) = n(6n - 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230354} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n) = (n + 1)(6n + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230355} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n) = n(6n + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230356} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n) = n(6n + 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230357}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186230352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=n(6n-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377373} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=n(6n+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377374} {:answer/type {:db/ident 